# gpt-5.4 second-attacker package (#9a): harness + baseline + gpt-5.4 answers + answer keys + scored summary.
# EXCLUDE the bulky batch_*.json prompt blobs (23M, dataset-derived, regenerable via scripts/cr_2afc_export.py).
!/gpt54_2afc_pkg/
/gpt54_2afc_pkg/tasks/*/batch_*.json

# gpt-5.4 second attacker on the FIXED cards (A2, cited certification).
#
# ⚠ CORRECTION (2026-08-15).  The exclusion below was written to mirror the older package's, but
# this package nests one level deeper (tasks/<dataset>/s<seed>/batch_*.json), so the single-`*`
# pattern never matched: 99 prompt blobs / 28.5 MB have been TRACKED and PUBLISHED since aac71fd.
# They contain the 2AFC prompts verbatim, i.e. the raw member writing samples the cards were
# distilled from.  Reviewed and DELIBERATELY KEPT:
#   - the underlying corpora are public (Mozilla/Apache bug trackers, the Enron corpus,
#     CrossValidated), so no non-public data is exposed by shipping them;
#   - keeping them makes the cited gpt-5.4 second-attacker certification independently
#     re-runnable, which regenerating-from-source would not (the raw datasets are not shipped).
# This is a RESEARCH REPRODUCTION package, not a deployment: the paper's deployment assumption
# (the card-building corpus stays private) is unaffected -- see README "Artifact vs deployment".
#
# The stale one-level exclusion is therefore REMOVED rather than fixed: config and reality now
# agree (these blobs are tracked, on purpose) instead of the config claiming an exclusion that
# git never applied.  The older package below keeps its exclusion -- that one does match.
!/gpt54_2afc_fixed_pkg/

# ============================================================================
# HARD DENY — must stay LAST so no whitelist rule above can re-include these.
# Per-line sanitize audit sidecars map card lines back to member text; they share
# the access level of raw member data and are NEVER shipped, in any directory.
# ============================================================================
*_audit.json
